Tests that a caller alias template's ordinary TYPE parameter which
shares its short name with a namespace-scope alias template used
inside another template's member alias does not capture that
template-name (N5008 [temp.names]/2): `__conditional_t`'s `_If`
parameter (bound to the in-progress class `vec<int>`) must not
substitute into conditional's `using type = _If<_Bp, int, _ElseRes>`
-- neither as the template-name (yielding nonsense
`vec<_Bp, int, _ElseRes>`) nor by wholesale replacement of the
template-id (yielding `vec<int>` and dropping the argument list).
Mirrors libc++'s __conditional_t/conditional pair as used by
vector's __trivially_relocatable member alias.
